# Source requirements documents are marked "Confidential - internal & supplier
# use" (FRD) and "Confidential - engineering" (TRS). They must never be
# committed to this repository.
docs/source/
*.docx
*.doc

# Ingested supplier material and generated workbooks are confidential per NFR-03
# (contract and pricing documents are access-restricted).
data/
corpus/
out/
*.xlsx
!tests/fixtures/**/*.xlsx

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
Icon?

# Agent working directory. Session transcripts, worktrees and local agent state -
# none of it is project source, and `.claude/worktrees/` holds whole checkouts.
#
# Ignored rather than merely "never staged": the rule was enforced by discipline
# for the whole of Phase 1, and one `git add -A` would have committed it. Every
# other confidential path here (docs/source/, data/, corpus/, out/, *.xlsx, .env*)
# was already covered; this was the gap.
.claude/
